    "question": "How long does it actually take for home solar panels to pay for themselves?",
    "summary": "The solar panel payback period — the time for electricity savings to recoup installation costs — typically ranged from 7 to 12 years for U.S. homeowners based on 2023–2024 data, with major variation driven by local electricity rates, sunlight availability, and incentives such as the federal 30%…",
